===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|de|gmh|rōst}}, from {{inh|de|goh|rōst}}, from {{der|de|gmw|*raust}}. Cognate with {{cog|dum|rôost}}, {{cog|osx|rōst}}. From Germanic stems {{cog|fro|rostir|t=to roast}}, whence {{cog|en|roast}}.

Alongside this masculine stood a feminine {{m+|gmh|rōste}}, {{m+|goh|rōsta}}, {{m+|gml|rôste}} (whence dated modern German {{m|de|Roste|g=f}}). Further the derived {{cog|nl|rooster}}, {{cog|gml|rôster}}, which is attested with all three genders. In contemporary German, {{m|de||Rost}} is alternatively construed as a neuter, probably driven by the desire to distinguish it from etymology 1 and perhaps by analogy with {{m|de|Blech|t=baking sheet}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|de|/ʁɔst/||standard}}
** {{audio|de|De-at-Rost.ogg|a=Austria}}
* {{IPA|de|/ʁoːst/|qq=alternatively in the south, else archaic}}

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m:n,es,e:^e}}

# [[grid]] {{gloss|number of parallel staffs}}
